WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.730
Now then...

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.820
It's time...

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.280
...to bring about some justice!

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.670
How...?!

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.970
Rosenthal Third Number, Huotou, activating.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:38.300
Danger to Adonai detected.
Commencing action to purge the danger.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.240
How is she moving around...?

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.200
Y-You...

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.030
You're supposed to be dead
as a result of our justice...!

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.200
S-Stay back!

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.540
No... What's here isn't just a body;

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.540
it's a person.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.540
Stay back, you monster!!

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.630
Attack identified.
Prioritizing charm damage avoidance.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.930
Permitting physical damage up to Level 4.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:27.190
Hey, man! Don't be so quick
to call others monsters.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:32.190
A real monster, you see...

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.610
...is more along the lines of <i>this</i>!

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:57.510
"A Certain Scientific Accelerator"

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:08.410
"#04 Third Number (The Pseudo-Soul, Huotou)"

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.000
You're done for now!

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.330
What a shame.
If I were in a slightly better mood,

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:16.710
there were a number of things
I would have asked you first.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:20.590
It makes no difference now, though.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.510
Even this babe in the woods here

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:26.430
is at least smart enough
to show respect for the dead,

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:31.520
but you seem to prefer cutting them up
and dissolving them, don't you?

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.480
If I'm being honest,
I'm not opposed to that, myself. So...

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.030
...let's you and me, monster to monster,

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.610
have a little fun with each other!

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.790
I'm thinking of using the blood flow
and bioelectricity in your body

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.000
and trying my hand at creating a little art.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.800
You'll be dead, though, 
and won't get to see it.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.390
Huh?

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.350
He got so freaked out, he lost consciousness.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.150
What a disgrace to villainy.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.480
Now...

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.270
...is it your turn next?

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.290
Wh-What is this?

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.460
What's wrong?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.330
Huh?

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:43.970
My wound has opened up again. Even so...

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.850
...it doesn't matter.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.810
Hey!

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.450
"Morgue"

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.470
Are you okay? Shake it off.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.140
Adonai...

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:32.680
...he has not sustained injury serious
enough to terminate life functions.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.560
By taking appropriate measures,
he should recover.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:41.520
Rescue teams should be arriving shortly.
Should we pursue him?

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.610
No. I can't leave him here like this.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:50.410
He is my essential...

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.830
Essential...?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.080
...t-teacher, actually.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.370
Teacher?

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:59.210
Yeah. I have much to learn from him.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.590
Move it! Move it!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.500
Out of the way!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.300
Move! Move!

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.880
Move!

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:21.150
"That kind of violence cannot be tolerated,"

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:25.030
says Misaka, issuing a warning.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.740
"Please run away from here at once,"

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:33.030
says Misaka, requesting evacuation
while keeping the villain occupied.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.700
Tch, damn it!

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.960
Misaka dodges him,

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.080
then deprives him of mobility
for several seconds using electricity,

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.880
while in the meantime...

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.920
Insulation?!

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.310
In that case, Misaka

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.980
makes an attempt at hacking.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:02.520
That uniform is from Tokiwadai.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:06.860
There is shielding in place.
But breaking in should still be possible.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:10.950
I don't know who you are, but I don't
need you using your abilities on me.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.240
Adonai, I have located him.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.880
Hey, hurry and get in!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:23.790
That means...

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.500
...you're my hostage!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:39.220
Pursuing.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.890
Huh? Are you sure you're all right?

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.900
I am unsure of your 
definition of "all right,"

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.270
but if I sacrifice 70% of
the muscle fiber in my legs,

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:51.070
I should catch up to them
in roughly 180 seconds.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.450
You can't.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.080
We'll pursue them once we're better prepared.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.160
I don't want to create any more unhappiness.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.920
This was made by an
Antiskill vehicle, all right.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.500
But vehicles of this type were all
supposed to have been disposed of.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.630
If this kind of vehicle was used...

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.130
Then sure enough...

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.760
It's those guys, isn't it?

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:17.760
DA strikes again.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.600
"Operating"

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:23.100
For goodness sake, what 
is it with my patients?

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.360
Why can't they ever seem to stay still?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:35.240
U-i-ha-ru!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:45.580
--Jeez, why do you always do that?!
--Okay, I'm sorry!

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:47.790
Setting that aside for now...

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.050
But you never really set it aside.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:52.170
...I heard the greatest story, you know?

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.470
Another urban legend?

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:58.260
Now, now, don't be like that.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:02.220
So anyway, somewhere
underneath Academy City,

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:05.440
there are subway trains running
that nobody has a solid grasp of,

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.770
and get this--one of them is the
"subway train that runs forever,"

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:12.650
which has never once
stopped at a single station!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:16.280
There you go again
with another half-baked rumor.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:18.820
I'm telling you, it's not half-baked!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.870
Somebody once saw it.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:30.790
The subway train that always runs isn't
even remotely like any other train.

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:33.050
Yes, as you wish.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.420
Can I ask you to wait just a moment, please?

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:46.230
Forgive me for interrupting
your dinner, Mr. Breeder.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:49.980
I believe at the moment,
you're passing under School District 7?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:54.860
Imagine, one of Academy City's top leaders
on a train that runs all the time...

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:59.110
Are you that afraid to allow
your location to be made known?

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:03.450
Feel free to call me Nakimoto now.
We may as well be open.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:08.460
And I will call you Hishigata,
instead of Dachshund.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.880
There's something I need
to speak to you about.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:11.920
What is it?

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.710
I don't want my plan to
be disrupted by small-timers.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:18.760
I already haven't obtained
something that I should have,

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:22.430
and I would hate to have any more
of my upcoming activities obstructed.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:26.060
I see. You're saying that 
DA is going too far?

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.350
That's what I'm saying.
We're on the same page.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.900
Indeed, having another
full-blown action in public view,

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:38.570
like that one at the healthcare facility,
would be hard to accept.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.110
In any event,

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:45.040
as a member of the city's governing board,
I appreciate your input.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:50.000
So I can look forward to
the situation improving, then?

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.580
Goodbye.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:59.090
Heh, I like an old man who gets my snark.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.890
DA...

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:09.060
As an organization with
technical skill and the ability to act,

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.770
I thought they would be of some use to me,

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:14.060
but apparently, they're too out of control.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.570
It may be about time to cut them out.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:20.650
This will be a good opportunity
to put Scavenger to the test.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:24.620
Are you sure? Like I always say,
once they're let loose on the world,

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.540
they're completely out of our hands.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:29.250
You really are sure about this?

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.790
Okay, okay!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.460
Okay! Okay! Okay!

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.500
Okay!

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.260
Okay, everyone, gather around.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.100
Eyes up here!

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.980
Time to go to work.

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:22.930
Dr. Matsumoto, from Internal Medicine,
please report to Exam Room 3, stat.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:28.850
Dr. Matsumoto, from Internal
Medicine, please report to Exam Room 3, stat.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:32.270
There's nothing wrong
with the hospital. Which means,

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:36.020
he ran the hell away without giving me
another thought after I collapsed.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:39.780
Damn it, these villains are
rotten through and through.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:43.700
Blondie isn't around, either.
Did she go after the guy who escaped?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:47.740
I doubt she's forgotten that
she's being chased after, as well.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.960
Ah, you're awake.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.040
"I was so worried, I made 
sure I stayed awake,

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.260
but when it really counted, I was asleep!"

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:05.840
says Misaka Misaka, caught up
in a terrible pang of regret!

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.320
Are you okay?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.860
Of course I am.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:25.900
"Do you want something to eat?"
asks Misaka Misaka, inwardly feeling uneasy,

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.160
afraid that you'll ask for an apple,

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:31.700
since she is unable to peel an apple,
and would be up a creek.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.250
No, I don't.

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:37.960
Actually, get me a can of coffee.
I take it black.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.840
There should be some in the
vending machine on the first floor.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.210
The doctor said stimulants 
would be a bad idea,

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.720
but in your case, it's sure to be medicinal!

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:49.430
Which is why Misaka Misaka
will go sneak down and buy some!

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:51.850
"Oh, come to think of it,

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:56.690
I don't have any money,"
says Misaka Misaka, staring you down,

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:00.650
waiting for you to hand over your money card.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:01.770
Thank you!

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.690
Okay, I'll go buy it!

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:11.580
So, what do <i>you</i> want?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:17.540
Are you here to laugh at the mess I am?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.920
"You look too pitiful to be called a mess,"

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:26.170
replies Misaka, gazing at you
who got hurt saving the host individual.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:32.050
I didn't do it to save all of you.
I just did it because I wanted to.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.060
Misaka is denying shared
memory access temporarily,

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.850
so that the host individual 
does not find out,

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.440
but it is only a matter of time.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.400
Here.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.730
What is it?

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:46.990
Misaka is in possession of a letter
for you from the blond foreign lady.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:51.070
"A civilian has been abducted.
Going to retrieve her"

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:51.450
What kind of penmanship is this?
Is she a kid? With <i>those</i> looks?

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.330
"Misaka wrote it down for her,"

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:58.330
answers Misaka, flummoxed by the
unexpected appraisal of her handwriting.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:01.790
Misaka feels self-assured based on
the knowledge gained from shojo manga

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:06.420
that having cute handwriting can
be effective when writing love letters.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:09.470
Abducted?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:12.850
The civilian individual stated
as being abducted is still unharmed.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.720
How can you know that?

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:19.640
"The civilian... is No. 10046," says Misaka,

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:23.730
disclosing the information
she declines to share with Last Order.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.360
What?

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:29.110
"Yoshikawa Kikyo"

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:36.040
Oh, you answered. I heard the
Frog Doctor had to take care of you again,

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:38.500
but I guess you're well enough
to answer your phone, huh?

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:42.920
Buzz off. I don't have time to waste, here.
State your business.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:46.670
I took the trouble to call you regarding
the matter you asked me about,

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:49.510
so maybe your treatment
of me is a little bit mean.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.970
Okay, so get on with it.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:54.550
The kid is gonna figure out
that something isn't right pretty soon.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:58.020
Something bad is happening
that involves her again, huh?

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.390
Well, okay.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:00.270
Tch.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:03.270
I learned a few things about DA.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:06.020
DA is an abbreviation for 
"Disciplinary Action,"

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.440
of the punitive measure variety.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:11.070
They're kind of like a
mutual aid society within Antiskill.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.320
At least, that's what they 
publicly claim to be,

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:17.240
but in actuality, they're a secret society.
And a fairly nasty one, at that.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:21.580
I know well enough that they're scum
and an insult to real villainy.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:27.340
Yes. They'll resort to anything to
bring about what they call their "justice."

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.590
It was started by members

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:32.590
who were reprimanded for carrying
their peacekeeping actions too far,

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:35.090
so maybe that's to be expected.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:39.060
The problem is, they have 
a lot of sympathizers.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.180
Sympathizers?

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:45.310
DA has grown with the help of members
and former members of Antiskill

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.360
who espouse the same ideals,

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:51.900
and who provide them with lots
of information, funding, and tech.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:55.950
When evil spreads,
it invites even more, powerful evil.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:59.080
In DA's case, that includes
powerful movers and shakers,

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.620
defense firms that ended up being rejected,

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:06.880
not to mention a dangerous neuroscientist.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:09.210
Scientist, huh?

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:13.720
On the other hand, one of the bigwigs
who had been showing favor to DA

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:17.760
must have thought that DA's
extreme actions were becoming a nuisance,

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:22.020
and apparently, just started
taking action to have them purged.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:27.440
As a result, there's whole lot of
danger looming around DA right now.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:28.940
Which is exactly why Antiskill,

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.610
which had been primarily
shut down by this bigwig up to now,

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:35.240
may be going into action against them.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:39.870
If you're planning to get involved in
this matter, make sure you're careful.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:43.500
None of that matters to me.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:48.710
If I don't like who or what someone is,
no matter who they may be, I kill them.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.630
That's all there is to it.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.880
Sorry to make you do this.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:18:01.060
It is not a problem. If I allocate
60% of my brain's capacity to this,

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:05.270
it is possible for me to raise
my sense of smell temporarily.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:08.020
Analysis complete. This way.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:10.060
All right, let's hurry.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.860
It appears some foolish evil
has gone into action.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:18.990
Nakimoto has done much to help our cause,

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:22.740
but apparently, he can no
longer understand our lofty ideals.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.700
Worldly snobs are always such an annoyance.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:28.040
I-Isn't it a bad idea to turn
the governing board against us?

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:30.580
What are you saying, you weakling?!

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:35.420
I thought we swore to eliminate all
our enemies for the cause of justice!

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.430
Fainthearted defeatists must be purged!

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.720
Fainthearted defeatists
must be purged!

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:43.390
Fainthearted defeatists must be purged.

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:46.390
S-Sorry, you're right.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.850
We <i>did</i> resolve to give up
our lives for the sake of justice.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.650
I-I admit I was wrong.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:58.490
No matter. We are now more than
equipped to oppose the governing board.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:03.370
This only means that the time has
come to use our power against all evil.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:07.750
Why don't we teach them a lesson
about the strength of our justice?

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:12.420
And in doing so, we'll bring
about true peace in Academy City!

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:15.670
Sheesh, these guys must have
nothing better to do. Mm-hmm.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:26.720
Ah, that reminds me. That idiot
who ran out in the middle of his mission

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:30.100
brought a hostage back
to the base, of all things.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:32.310
I want her. Would you mind?

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:35.190
All right. I'll have her sent to you.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.030
Thanks a lot, mm-hmm.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:40.780
But why do you seek that individual?

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:43.280
For the cause of justice, of course.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:46.830
I'm not interested in
anything other than justice.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:56.710
The more I investigate, the more
they come out of the woodwork.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:20:02.470
DA is a nest of terrorists.
Why did none of this ever come out before,

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:05.350
but now, the information
is suddenly showing up?

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:09.100
And from what I'm seeing,
the equipment DA has

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:12.230
is slightly superior to Antiskill's
state-of-the-art stuff.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:17.150
We'd best consider them to be
a significantly dangerous organization.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.860
What is an Antiskill member who went missing

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:22.820
after his extreme subjugation of
a student left them half-paralyzed

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.030
doing in this lineup?

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:29.870
This one illegally diverted Antiskill
weapons and was dismissed.

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.830
I remember he sent them
to a hostile organization,

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.000
with the goal of wiping out
terrorists, or something.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:39.590
It's almost as though the dark underbelly
of Antiskill is assembled here...

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:47.350
Explosion at a warehouse in the 3rd District!

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.520
"Estimated scope of DA hideouts"
"3rd District warehouse area, Warehouse 5"

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.690
So are we done earning some spare change?

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:55.650
Did you get a complete headcount?

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:59.530
Aww... As completely
wiped out as this place is,

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:02.900
wouldn't that usually mean the job is over?

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:07.120
This isn't the only target location;
was this everyone?

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:11.160
Did anyone see someone carrying
a bag big enough to stick a girl inside?

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:12.120
There, you see?

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.330
You're kidding me!

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.130
Listen, this is business.

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:20.590
We've been hired to eradicate
this "DA" organization entirely.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:23.050
If we fail to kill any targets,

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.550
forget about small change,
it'll be breach of contract.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:28.720
Wah! So, what do we do?

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:38.650
It's okay, it's okay. Do you think a mere
human can escape from my Predator?

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:55.000
Heh, your ability always
smacks of some clammy stalker.

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:01.800
Found you.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:36.950
"Next time"

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:41.530
"DA"
